Which equation represents the graphed semicircle, centred at the origin?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.35]
\draw[<->] (-9,0)--(9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-9)--(0,1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue] (-8,0) arc (180:360:8);
\fill (-8,0) circle (2pt) node[above] {$-8$};
\fill (8,0) circle (2pt) node[above] {$8$};
\node[below left] at (0,-8) {$-8$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What are the domain and range of the semicircle shown?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.3]
\draw[<->] (-10,0)--(1,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-10)--(0,10) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,9) arc (90:270:9);
\fill (0,-9) circle (2pt) node[right] {$-9$};
\fill (0,9) circle (2pt) node[right] {$9$};
\node[below left] at (-9,0) {$-9$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which equation represents the semicircle shown, centred at the origin?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.45]
\draw[<->] (-7,0)--(7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1)--(0,7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue] (6,0) arc (0:180:6);
\fill (-6,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$-6$};
\fill (6,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$6$};
\node[above left] at (0,6) {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
